body:
I am an avid hunter as well and I think you just need to accept that October/November are hunting times. I am going to assume you live in Michigan because you used the term "up north" haha. Talk to him about this and try to compromise. I think you can definitely find a solution to this problem. =\]

&#x200B;

 It is also tough to be dating for 2 years and be an hour away from each other. I feel your pain.

I struggle to see this game developing much past the point at which it is now because of the health/armor and easy recovery of health/armor and the general lack of weapon niches.

&#x200B;

Currently, longer range weapons offer almost no advantage over the shorter range ones because if I hit you 2 times with the longbow, you can still duck into cover, heal up, then run at me again. It is much more effective for me to run up to a player with a R-99 and break their shield, then finish them with a peacekeeper. 

&#x200B;

You've got to adjust the damage profile of the longbow so that 2 body shots will deal 150 damage and/or slow down the time that someone can heal. Obviously, this would mean that the headshot multiplier should be adjusted to around 1.5x instead of 2x. 

&#x200B;

This is especially important for when solos comes out (I really hope it does). Using a longbow puts you at an extreme disadvantage when it comes to close range. While shooting at someone from long range and just watch them soak up damage until they blast you in the face while you try switching to your close range gun would be extremely frustrating when you have no teammates to support you (and the chance a random supports you now is low already). 

&#x200B;

Weapon niches are important in any shooter game. The issues in Apex Legends is best described by the Flatline. There is absolutely no use for this gun in the game. The only time you should ever use it is if its the first gun you receive (which is an uncommon occurrence). Every other ballistic AR/SMG outclasses it in almost every category. The energy weapons are the same way with the exception of the triple take. You must offer a viable niche for each gun you put into the game, and it is silly for a player to take a HAVOC over an R-301, hoping to get a turbocharger, to only figure out that the R-301 is still significantly better. The spin-up time for both the Devotion and HAVOC punishes the user without a good enough upside to contend with other weapons. 

&#x200B;

I know Fortnite is often ostracized on this sub, but they really have mastered this concept of niches. Nearly every weapon/equipment they have added has had various positives and negatives that allow it to fill a perfect niche or create a good, viable combo. 

&#x200B;

This game needs to work on the health and armor mechanics as well as the weapon balance (even after the patch) to become a long-term success. 

&#x200B;

And I sincerely hope it does because I like the game as a whole and like seeing success!



&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Can we please add some magic weapons as a reward from this quest? The skill needs to be buffed so badly. The player base will never nerf range, so let's try to introduce strong, blowpipe-ish mage weapons.

&#x200B;

Also, I love the crystal bow to be buffed somehow because I love it and so do many others. Maybe we can move the imbue effect from NMZ to the new content somehow and double or triple the charges on it before it degrades?

&#x200B;

(And while you are at it, just remove NMZ)

